reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4}{7}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =3\\cdot x+(-2)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319255" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319255" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-15606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=13$ and the angle between vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $\\theta = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/example-15606.json" "file_sha256" "0e9c6d7a5c47e04989feaab67ef94c4196f6bde2cf1929d9ced123cf16f09615" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-15606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =13\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/example-15606.json" "file_sha256" "0e9c6d7a5c47e04989feaab67ef94c4196f6bde2cf1929d9ced123cf16f09615" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-15607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,3,-1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,-7,0 \\rangle.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/example-15607.json" "file_sha256" "8b6383a6068ca2a0b35ef19117fe4b2882e1557807c6053e7d78b7dbb453b8e6" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-15607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-7)+(-1)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{53}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/example-15607.json" "file_sha256" "8b6383a6068ca2a0b35ef19117fe4b2882e1557807c6053e7d78b7dbb453b8e6" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-15608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/example-15608.json" "file_sha256" "3cfe30534bdf4e233a568d0b0af2a64f57c981c4d676d167a2e79ca6d03deb96" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-15608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{c}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/example-15608.json" "file_sha256" "3cfe30534bdf4e233a568d0b0af2a64f57c981c4d676d167a2e79ca6d03deb96" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-318964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $|\\,k\\,|=2\\sqrt{2}$ and the angle between vectors $k$ and $l$ is $\\theta ={120}^{∘}.$ Find the scalar projection of $k$ onto $l.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{l}\\,k=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "7669e053737b969ef851cac018c6723dff19eb302f201dcbb6c5526941f37aad"} {"question" "q-318964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{l}\\,k & =|\\,k\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({120}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/state.json" "file_sha256" "7669e053737b969ef851cac018c6723dff19eb302f201dcbb6c5526941f37aad"} {"question" "q-318964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "116abfe154838a6164d2dc5466f4720d03ebc4992780a9c9dbe8b22a380f4e02"} {"question" "q-318964" "